"""Rooms, driven end to end: a persona room through a REAL subprocess, a library room through real HTTP.

`AgentSettings.executable` points at `tests/support/fake_agent_cli.py`, so the
kit's driver spawns a genuine child exactly as it would spawn `claude`, and
this suite asserts on the argv and environment the kit builds for this app
rather than on a mock. A library room's `LibraryAgent` asks
`tests/support/fake_library.py` over the api-clients `library` client, the
library's caller door faked at its routes.

A turn is a task that outlives its request, writing on its own connection,
so this suite commits for real: its `client` overrides nothing, and every
test is a fresh person (`_person`), so no two share a row or an allowance.
httpx's ASGI transport hands back a response only once it is whole, so an
ask left running is a task (`_asking`), and cancelling it is the tab closing.
"""

